ause **the engines are the source of the power that makes the climb possible.** * If you are in a car and you go up a steep hill, you hear the engine rev higher. You don't say, "The engine is lifting the car," you say, "The engine is working harder to get us up the hill." * It is the exact same thing in a plane. The engines are "working harder" to provide the energy to climb, but the **wings** are the surface that is actually pushing against the air to generate the lift that carries you upward. **To summarize:** * **Without the wings,** the engines would just be rockets pushing you forward in a straight line. * **Without the engines,** the wings would just be gliders slowly falling to the ground. You need both. The engines provide the **power** (the roar), and the wings provide the **lift** (the climb). You are feeling the "power" part of the equation, which is why your brain correctly associates the loud noise with going up!
